{
  "template": "wireframes",
  "title": "Borders around the photo: wireframes",
  "intro": "How borders look and work in Develop, in Recipes and at export, from the design (docs/plans/borders.md) and the tracker rows BRD-3, BRD-4 and EXP-5. Built on the borders branch, not yet on main.",
  "updated": "2026-10-16T08:30:00+01:00",
  "reading": "Boxes are regions, numbers point to the notes under each wireframe, and sizes in the examples are made up. Every region says where it stands:",
  "statuses": {
    "planned": {
      "meaning": "In the tracker for this release; its engine may exist without its panel."
    },
    "later": {
      "meaning": "After this release."
    },
    "you": {
      "meaning": "Waiting on a measurement or a decision of yours."
    }
  },
  "flow": [
    {
      "title": "Choose a look",
      "text": "A Base Look, a mood or your own adjustments, as today; none of them touches the border.",
      "status": "built"
    },
    {
      "title": "Pick a border",
      "text": "Hover the Borders folder in Recipes to preview White 4:5, a gallery mat or a film frame on the photo, and click one.",
      "status": "building"
    },
    {
      "title": "Fine-tune it",
      "text": "The Border panel: shape, orientation, size, position, colour and a keyline.",
      "status": "building"
    },
    {
      "title": "Export",
      "text": "As edited, without the border for a lab, or with a Borders recipe on every photo; sizes include the border.",
      "status": "building"
    }
  ],
  "principles": [
    {
      "title": "Around, never over",
      "text": "The canvas grows to the shape; nothing of the photo is hidden, as with Lightroom Classic's Print to JPEG."
    },
    {
      "title": "Apart from looks",
      "text": "Moods and looks don't set or reset the border, and a border recipe doesn't touch the look."
    },
    {
      "title": "Relative to the photo",
      "text": "Sizes are shares of the photo, so a border reads the same at 1080 pixels and at full size."
    },
    {
      "title": "The photo is still judged alone",
      "text": "The histogram, clipping, crop and colour-assessment view ignore the border; the panel's switch hides it."
    }
  ],
